---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';
---

<Base title="About">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      I'm {SITE.name}, also known online as <code>{SITE.handle}</code>. I do security research with a focus on
      reverse engineering and software protection.
    </p>

    <h2>What I work on</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Reverse engineering &amp; software protection:</strong> .NET internals, obfuscators and code virtualizers, anti-tamper and licensing schemes.</li>
      <li><strong>Offensive security:</strong> authorized penetration testing, web application security and Windows internals.</li>
      <li><strong>Malware analysis &amp; incident response.</strong></li>
      <li><strong>AI-assisted security research:</strong> agent-driven analysis pipelines with verifiable, provenance-checked output.</li>
      <li><strong>Quantitative finance &amp; ML:</strong> systematic trading research and machine learning projects.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How I work</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>I only test what I'm authorized to test, with a written scope.</li>
      <li>Client findings stay with the client. Product-level flaws go to the vendor through <a href="/disclosure-policy/">coordinated disclosure</a>.</li>
      <li>Public write-ups never include client-identifying details or working exploits for unfixed issues.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Work with me</h2>
    <p>
      I take on authorized protection assessments and security audits. Reach out via the
      <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
